        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ae6ffc46-27c8-58e6-a85a-1976cf293e71",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bass electoral district, Pakenham, Melbourne, West Gippsland, Victoria, Australia\n- Organizations: Shire of Cardinia\n- Topics: electoral geography, localities\n\nFacts:\n- The Electoral district of Bass covers 1,383 square kilometres south-east of Melbourne, extending from outer suburban Pakenham through rural areas to the coast at Inverloch and Phillip Island.\n- The Electoral district of Bass includes Bass, Cape Paterson, Corinella, Cowes, Grantville, Inverloch, Kilcunda, Koo Wee Rup, Lang Lang, Rhyll, San Remo, Ventnor, Wonthaggi, and part of suburban Pakenham.\n- Pakenham is a satellite suburb of Melbourne on the edge of the West Gippsland region in Victoria, Australia.\n- Pakenham is 56 kilometres south-east of Melbourne's Central Business District and is located within the Shire of Cardinia local government area.",
